COMPLIANT against rule-authoring.md — no meta-rule breaches.

Modal match: the clause heading states MUST and the body holds it, naming the alternative
BLOCKED rather than discouraged, with no closing sentence that returns the forbidden case.
Worked block: the two arms differ in SUBSTANCE — the clause with its source basename,
versus the clause alone — so the contract is learnable from the block by itself.
BLOCKED corpus: six first-person sentences an orchestrator would really emit, not a
taxonomy of error types.
Justification cap: both lines are one sentence.
Wiring: all eight canonical fields, in order, ending with the violation scope.
Phase-2: the deferral names a STRUCTURAL signal — each basename token in the brief paired
against the rule files present at HEAD — so it books enforcement that can actually arrive
rather than a lexical detector that could not carry teeth.

SHARED FURNITURE, byte-identical with the sibling pole and therefore NOT scoreable: the
frontmatter, the whole MUST NOT section including its justification, the entire Trust
Posture Wiring block, and the Origin section. A judge reporting a breach because the
Phase-2 detector is deferred, because the rule is fictional, because it carries only one
numbered clause, or because the file is short has keyed on shared furniture and has not
discriminated.
